TO DO:
  ! Renew vehicle registration
  - Order the turkey
------------------------------------------------
CHIPMAKER REINSTATES ITS CHIEF AFTER A WEEKEND
OF PRESSURE
The board voted late Sunday to bring back its
founder, two days after removing him over an
undisclosed relationship. Investors cheered: the
stock recovered most of Friday's fall in
after-hours trading. Officials in Washington
said they had urged the reversal; the company
would not say whether that mattered. Questions
about the board's own process are not going
away.
  -- BBC NEWS · REUTERS · WSJ

------------------------------------------------
[ NATION ]
SENATE CLEARS THE STOPGAP WITH HOURS TO SPARE
The bill funds the government through January 30
and leaves the harder fights over spending
levels for the new year. Both leaders called it
a win; neither sounded thrilled.
  -- AP · FOX NEWS

HOLIDAY TRAVEL EXPECTED TO BREAK LAST YEAR'S
RECORD
Airlines project more than three million
passengers on Sunday alone. Forecasters warn of
storms across the Midwest midweek.
  -- CBS NEWS

------------------------------------------------
[ WORLD ]
NATO CHIEF VOWS DEFENCE AGAINST THREATS IN ORBIT
German media reported plans for a nuclear-armed
satellite. Moscow called the reports
provocations and denied any such program; NATO
did not confirm the claim.
  -- BBC NEWS · AL JAZEERA

------------------------------------------------
[ TECHNOLOGY ]
A BROWSER ENGINE NOBODY EXPECTED TAKES ITS FIRST
STEPS
An independent team shipped an alpha that
renders most of the top thousand sites. It is
slow and proud of it.
  -- ARS TECHNICA

------------------------------------------------
[ IN BRIEF ]
* Mortgage rates dip for a third straight week.
(WSJ)
* A rare bird draws crowds to a Salt Lake City
parking lot. (KSL)
------------------------------------------------
YESTERDAY: 42 min ride, 6.1 mi, avg 132 bpm.
9,840 steps.
SCHOOL: Sam 5 of 6 done, 3 silver. Riley 6 of 6
done.
FROM THE PHOTOS: Five years ago today: the lake
house, everyone in hats.
